        "Welcome to Day 52 of 3D Computer Graphics, WebGL2 & GPU Shader Architecture. Today we advance from fluid dynamics to deformable surface mechanics: Position Based Dynamics (PBD) & Extended PBD (XPBD) for Cloth, Hair & Soft-Body Simulation.",
        "In classical physics engines, physical bodies were simulated using Force-Based Formulations (such as mass-spring-damper systems). In a mass-spring system, when a cloth edge stretches, Hooke's Law calculates a restorative force F = -k * (x - x_0) - d * v. While force-based springs are simple to understand conceptually, they suffer from a fatal flaw known as The Stiffness Problem. If you simulate an inelastic material\u2014such as heavy denim jeans, leather armor, or a silk banner\u2014you must set the spring stiffness k to an extraordinarily high value. Under explicit numerical integration, high spring stiffness introduces immense acceleration spikes that cause the simulation to violently explode unless you shrink the time step to microseconds!",
